    "label": "40",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following, expressing your answer with positive exponents. $\\left(\\dfrac{64a^3}{27b^9}\\right)^{\\frac13}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{4a}{3b^3}$, $b\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{64a^3}{27b^9}\\right)^{\\frac13}&=\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{64}\\,\\sqrt[3]{a^3}}{\\sqrt[3]{27}\\,\\sqrt[3]{b^9}}\\\\\\left(\\frac{64a^3}{27b^9}\\right)^{\\frac13}&=\\frac{4a}{3b^3}\\end{align*}$$The original denominator requires $b\\ne0$.",
